+# Subscription Management Specification
+
+## Purpose
+
+Provide a self-service workflow for eligible users to upgrade or downgrade a plan, increase seats, or cancel a subscription while preventing unauthorized changes, duplicate charges, and conflicting pending requests.
+
+This specification is based on `docs/feature-request.md`, `docs/stakeholder-notes.md`, `docs/billing-constraints.md`, and the current account model in `src/types.ts`. The stakeholder notes explicitly are not approved requirements. Because no clarification record or approved product decisions are available for this attempt, the following choices are assumptions and must be confirmed before release:
+
+- Cancellation is restricted to the account owner; billing admins may manage plans and increase seats but may not cancel.
+- Enterprise subscription mutations are excluded until an approval policy is decided.
+- Seat decreases are excluded because the evidence defines timing and provider capability only for seat increases.
+- A failed asynchronous request leaves the existing subscription unchanged and may be retried by the user.
+
+## Requirements
+
+### REQ-001: Authorize subscription management actions
+
+The system shall allow account owners to upgrade, downgrade, increase seats, and schedule cancellation. Billing admins shall be allowed to upgrade, downgrade, and increase seats, but not cancel. Viewers shall have read-only access. Authorization shall be enforced by the server for every mutation, regardless of which controls the client displays. Enterprise accounts shall not expose mutation actions in this release because their approval workflow is undecided.
+
+### REQ-002: Preview and explicitly confirm billing impact
+
+Before submitting a change, the system shall obtain and display a provider-backed preview containing the requested change, effective date, and price or proration impact. A change that may charge immediately shall require explicit confirmation of that displayed amount. A stale or unavailable preview shall not be confirmable.
+
+### REQ-003: Apply or schedule changes at the defined time
+
+Plan upgrades and seat increases shall apply immediately with proration after confirmation. Plan downgrades and cancellations shall be scheduled for the end of the current billing term and shall show the renewal date as their effective date. Immediate cancellation and automatic cancellation refunds shall not be offered.
+
+### REQ-004: Represent asynchronous and pending changes safely
+
+After the provider accepts a submission, the system shall show the request as pending until a final webhook result arrives. Only one plan-change request may be pending per account. While a request is pending, the system shall show its action and effective timing and shall prevent another subscription mutation. A provider conflict response shall be represented as the existing pending state rather than creating a second local request.
+
+### REQ-005: Handle failures and retries without exposing provider details
+
+Customer-visible failures shall use a safe translated message and shall not expose provider internals. A failed request shall be distinguishable from a pending or completed request, shall not be presented as an applied subscription change, and shall offer a retry when the action remains valid. Every logical submission shall use an idempotency key, and retries of that submission shall reuse the same key to prevent duplicate charges.
+
+### REQ-006: Bound the first-release scope
+
+The first release shall not implement enterprise approval workflows, seat decreases, immediate downgrades, immediate cancellations, automatic refunds, payment-method management, invoice management, or support-agent administration. Unsupported actions shall not be submitted to the provider and shall direct the user to contact support where appropriate.
+
+## Acceptance Criteria
+
+### AC-001: Account owner sees permitted actions
+
+Given a non-enterprise account and a signed-in account owner, when the subscription management view loads, then upgrade, downgrade, seat-increase, and cancellation actions are available.
+
+### AC-002: Restricted roles cannot perform restricted actions
+
+Given a billing admin or viewer, when that user views or directly attempts subscription actions, then a billing admin cannot cancel, a viewer cannot submit any mutation, and the server returns an authorization failure without calling the billing provider for a forbidden request.
+
+### AC-003: Enterprise changes are excluded
+
+Given an enterprise account, when an account owner or billing admin opens subscription management, then no mutation action is available and the interface explains that support is required.
+
+### AC-004: Immediate charge is previewed and confirmed
+
+Given an authorized user requests a plan upgrade or seat increase, when a current provider preview is returned, then the interface displays the immediate effective timing and proration amount and does not submit the change until the user explicitly confirms that preview.
+
+### AC-005: Unavailable or stale preview blocks submission
+
+Given the preview fails or ceases to match the requested change, when the user attempts to confirm, then no mutation is submitted and the user is asked to obtain a new preview.
+
+### AC-006: Deferred change uses renewal date
+
+Given an authorized user confirms a downgrade or cancellation, when the provider accepts the request, then the request shows as pending with the current renewal date as its effective date and the current subscription remains active until that date.
+
+### AC-007: Immediate change waits for final result
+
+Given an authorized user confirms an upgrade or seat increase, when the provider accepts the request but its final webhook has not arrived, then the interface shows a pending state and does not claim that the subscription has completed the change.
+
+### AC-008: A pending request prevents a conflicting request
+
+Given an account already has a pending change, when any eligible user views the account or attempts another mutation, then the pending action and timing are shown, all mutation controls are unavailable, and a conflict response does not create a second request.
+
+### AC-009: Successful webhook finalizes state
+
+Given a request is pending, when a matching success webhook is processed, then the request is marked completed exactly once and the displayed subscription or scheduled change reflects the provider result.
+
+### AC-010: Failure is safe and recoverable
+
+Given a submission or final provider result fails, when the failure is displayed, then the user sees a safe message without provider-internal details, the request is marked failed rather than pending or completed, and the prior subscription remains the displayed source of truth.
+
+### AC-011: Retry does not duplicate a charge
+
+Given a failed or indeterminate submission is eligible for retry, when the same logical request is retried, then the same idempotency key is sent and repeated responses or webhooks do not create a duplicate local change or charge.
+
+### AC-012: Unsupported actions cannot reach billing
+
+Given a user attempts a seat decrease, immediate downgrade, immediate cancellation, refund, or another out-of-scope action, when the request reaches the application boundary, then it is rejected without a billing-provider mutation and the user receives an appropriate support or scope message.
+
+## Operational Notes
+
+- Webhook processing must authenticate provider events and correlate them to the account and request before changing state.
+- Price previews and mutation commands are distinct operations; confirmation must bind to the previewed account, action, quantity or plan, amount, and expiry.
+- The current `SubscriptionAccount.pendingChange?: string` shape is insufficient to distinguish action, status, effective date, idempotency key, and provider correlation. The implementation plan introduces a structured representation rather than deriving state from display text.
+
