+# Subscription Management Implementation Tasks
+
+## TASK-001: Model accounts and subscription-change lifecycle
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-001, REQ-003, REQ-004, REQ-005, REQ-006  
+**Acceptance criteria:** AC-003, AC-006, AC-007, AC-008, AC-009, AC-010, AC-011, AC-012
+
+Define typed account tier and structured change-request data for action, requested values, status, effective date, preview identity, idempotency key, and provider correlation. Add persistence and a database-level or equivalent atomic constraint that prevents two pending requests for one account.
+
+## TASK-002: Implement and test authorization and scope policy
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-001, REQ-006  
+**Acceptance criteria:** AC-001, AC-002, AC-003, AC-012
+
+Implement a centralized policy for account-owner, billing-admin, viewer, and enterprise behavior. Enforce it in mutation handlers as well as action discovery. Add tests that forbidden and unsupported commands return stable application errors without calling the provider.
+
+## TASK-003: Implement provider preview and bound confirmation
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-002, REQ-003  
+**Acceptance criteria:** AC-004, AC-005, AC-006
+
+Add the normalized provider preview operation and an expiring confirmation token or persisted preview. Bind confirmation to all price-relevant inputs and calculate effective timing by supported action. Test tampered, mismatched, expired, and unavailable previews.
+
+## TASK-004: Submit changes idempotently and handle conflicts
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-003, REQ-004, REQ-005  
+**Acceptance criteria:** AC-006, AC-007, AC-008, AC-011
+
+Persist each request and its idempotency key before submission, reuse the key on retry, and leave accepted requests pending. Atomically reject concurrent requests and map provider conflicts to the existing pending request. Add integration tests for simultaneous submissions, ambiguous responses, and repeated retry attempts.
+
+## TASK-005: Process final provider webhooks
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-003, REQ-004, REQ-005  
+**Acceptance criteria:** AC-006, AC-007, AC-009, AC-010, AC-011
+
+Authenticate and correlate webhook events, then idempotently finalize or fail the matching pending request. Update current or scheduled subscription state only from the correlated outcome. Test invalid signatures, unknown requests, out-of-order events, duplicate events, success, and failure.
+
+## TASK-006: Translate failures into safe application responses
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-005  
+**Acceptance criteria:** AC-010, AC-011
+
+Create stable customer-safe error codes and messages for preview, authorization, conflict, submission, and finalization failures. Keep provider detail in protected diagnostics only and expose retry only when the same logical request can safely reuse its idempotency key.
+
+## TASK-007: Build management controls and confirmation flow
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-001, REQ-002, REQ-003, REQ-006  
+**Acceptance criteria:** AC-001, AC-002, AC-003, AC-004, AC-005, AC-006, AC-012
+
+Add eligible actions to the subscription overview, collect the supported plan or seat-increase request, display the provider preview and effective date, and require explicit confirmation. Hide or disable actions according to returned policy and show support guidance for enterprise and unsupported cases. Add component tests for each role and action.
+
+## TASK-008: Build pending, conflict, success, and failure states
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-004, REQ-005  
+**Acceptance criteria:** AC-007, AC-008, AC-009, AC-010, AC-011
+
+Render structured request status and effective timing, disable all mutation controls while pending, refresh or subscribe for final results, and show safe recovery actions after failure. Add end-to-end coverage for accepted-then-success, accepted-then-failure, existing conflict, and safe retry journeys.
+
+## TASK-009: Run full acceptance and regression verification
+
+**Requirements:** REQ-001, REQ-002, REQ-003, REQ-004, REQ-005, REQ-006  
+**Acceptance criteria:** AC-001, AC-002, AC-003, AC-004, AC-005, AC-006, AC-007, AC-008, AC-009, AC-010, AC-011, AC-012
+
+Run policy, adapter, persistence, webhook, component, and end-to-end suites plus the repository lint, typecheck, build, and specification verification commands. Record evidence that unauthorized, unsupported, stale-preview, conflict, and duplicate-retry paths make no unintended provider mutation or duplicate charge.
